#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0492 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "EXPANSION ARITHMETIC: two captures (SHIFT1, SHIFT2) => two tuples => two expansions, each fires, and the harness AGGREGATES. Count-only, NO #expectViolationAt - both violations come from datasetBroadcastResult at internal row 0 (reported row 1), and each carries only its own expansion's Output_Variable, so a row=1 SHIFTn=... pin could also match the other expansion's violation through the matcher's documented fallback."
#expectViolationCount 2
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col SHIFT1  type=Char
col SHIFT2  type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | NORMAL to HIGH | HIGH to NORMAL
